  "body": "## Summary\nThe missing emergency exit in `contracts/CLGauge/GaugeCL.sol:188` will cause an indefinite loss of access for CL gauge stakers as the gauge admin can toggle emergency mode and block the only withdraw path.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nIn `contracts/CLGauge/GaugeCL.sol:188` the `withdraw` function is guarded by the `isNotEmergency()` modifier, and there is no alternative withdrawal route exposed to users while `emergency` is `true`. This differs from the V2 gauge design, where `emergencyWithdraw` remains callable during emergencies. As a result, once `emergency` is activated, every user withdrawal reverts and NFTs remain custodied by the gauge until governance clears the flag.\n\n## Vulnerable path\n\n```solidity\nmodifier isNotEmergency() {\n    require(emergency == false, \"emergency\");\n    _;\n}\n```\nThis modifier blocks any function when `emergency` is active.\n\n```solidity\nfunction withdraw(uint256 tokenId, uint8 redeemType) external nonReentrant isNotEmergency {\n    require(_stakes[msg.sender].contains(tokenId), \"NA\");\n    // ...\n}\n```\nWhen stakers call `withdraw`, the modifier executes first; if `emergency` is `true`, the call reverts before the NFT can be returned.\n\n```solidity\nfunction activateEmergencyMode() external onlyOwner {\n    require(emergency == false, \"emergency\");\n    emergency = true;\n}\n```\nThe gauge owner (governance) can flip `emergency` on at any time, permanently trapping all staked NFTs until they later call `stopEmergencyMode`.\n\n## impact\n\nUsers cannot recover their liquidity NFTs while emergency mode is active, leaving funds inaccessible for the entire pause window.\n\n\n## Mitigation\n\nAdd an emergency withdrawal path that bypasses pool interactions and the `isNotEmergency` check, mirroring the V2 gauge pattern. For example:\n\n```solidity\nfunction emergencyWithdraw(uint256 tokenId) external nonReentrant {\n    require(emergency, \"EMER\");\n    require(_stakes[msg.sender].contains(tokenId), \"NA\");\n\n    _stakes[msg.sender].remove(tokenId);\n    nonfungiblePositionManager.safeTransferFrom(address(this), msg.sender, tokenId);\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {C4PoCTestbed} from \"./C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\nimport {HybraTimeLibrary} from \"../contracts/libraries/HybraTimeLibrary.sol\";\nimport {GaugeCL} from \"../contracts/CLGauge/GaugeCL.sol\";\nimport {INonfungiblePositionManager} from \"../contracts/CLGauge/interface/INonfungiblePositionManager.sol\";\nimport {Bribe} from \"../contracts/Bribes.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/ERC20.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721Receiver.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title C4PoC\n * @notice A complete deployment of the CL contract suite\n * @dev All available variables are showcased in the commented\n *      storage slots of the contract.\n */\n\ncontract C4PoC is C4PoCTestbed {\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n        if (address(bribeFactoryV3.gaugeManager()) == address(0)) {\n            bribeFactoryV3.initialize(\n                address(voter),\n                address(gaugeManager),\n                address(permissionsRegistry),\n                address(tokenHandler)\n            );\n        }\n    }\n\n    function test_CLGaugeEmergencyModeLocksWithdrawals() external {\n        address alice = makeAddr(\"alice-cl-gauge\");\n\n        MockERC20 token0 = new MockERC20(\"Mock Token 0\", \"MT0\");\n        MockERC20 token1 = new MockERC20(\"Mock Token 1\", \"MT1\");\n        MockCLPool mockPool = new MockCLPool(address(token0), address(token1));\n        MockCLFactory mockFactory = new MockCLFactory(address(mockPool));\n        MockNFPM mockNfpm = new MockNFPM(address(mockFactory));\n\n        MockERC20 rewardToken = new MockERC20(\"Reward Token\", \"RWD\");\n        MockRHYBR mockRhybr = new MockRHYBR();\n\n        GaugeCL gauge = new GaugeCL(\n            address(rewardToken),\n            address(mockRhybr),\n            address(this),\n            address(mockPool),\n            address(this),\n            address(0x1234),\n            address(0x5678),\n            true,\n            address(mockNfpm),\n            address(this)\n        );\n\n        uint128 liquidity = 1_000;\n        int24 tickSpacing = 60;\n        int24 tickLower = -300;\n        int24 tickUpper = 300;\n\n        uint256 tokenId = mockNfpm.mintPosition(\n            alice,\n            address(token0),\n            address(token1),\n            tickSpacing,\n            tickLower,\n            tickUpper,\n            liquidity\n        );\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        mockNfpm.setApprovalForAll(address(gauge), true);\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        gauge.deposit(tokenId);\n\n        assertEq(mockNfpm.ownerOf(tokenId), address(gauge), \"gauge should hold NFT after deposit\");\n\n        gauge.activateEmergencyMode();\n\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        vm.expectRevert(bytes(\"emergency\"));\n        gauge.withdraw(tokenId, 0);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        assertEq(mockNfpm.ownerOf(tokenId), address(gauge), \"NFT remains locked while emergency active\");\n\n        gauge.stopEmergencyMode();\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        gauge.withdraw(tokenId, 0);\n\n        assertEq(mockNfpm.ownerOf(tokenId), alice, \"user regains NFT after emergency cleared\");\n        assertEq(uint256(mockPool.stakedLiquidity()), 0, \"staked liquidity should be zero post-withdrawal\");\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockERC20 is ERC20 {\n    constructor(string memory name_, string memory symbol_) ERC20(name_, symbol_) {}\n\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        _mint(to, amount);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockCLFactory {\n    address public immutable pool;\n\n    constructor(address _pool) {\n        pool = _pool;\n    }\n\n    function getPool(address, address, int24) external view returns (address) {\n        return pool;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockCLPool {\n    address public immutable token0Address;\n    address public immutable token1Address;\n    uint128 private totalLiquidity;\n    uint256 private lastUpdatedTimestamp;\n\n    constructor(address token0_, address token1_) {\n        token0Address = token0_;\n        token1Address = token1_;\n    }\n\n    function updateRewardsGrowthGlobal() external {\n        lastUpdatedTimestamp = block.timestamp;\n    }\n\n    function getRewardGrowthInside(int24, int24, uint256) external pure returns (uint256) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    function lastUpdated() external view returns (uint256) {\n        return lastUpdatedTimestamp;\n    }\n\n    function rewardGrowthGlobalX128() external pure returns (uint256) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    function rewardReserve() external pure returns (uint256) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    function stakedLiquidity() external view returns (uint128) {\n        return totalLiquidity;\n    }\n\n    function stake(int128 delta, int24, int24, bool) external {\n        if (delta >= 0) {\n            totalLiquidity += uint128(uint256(int256(delta)));\n        } else {\n            uint128 amount = uint128(uint256(int256(-delta)));\n            require(totalLiquidity >= amount, \"insufficient liquidity\");\n            totalLiquidity -= amount;\n        }\n    }\n\n    function syncReward(uint256, uint256, uint256 periodFinish) external {\n        lastUpdatedTimestamp = periodFinish;\n    }\n\n    function rollover() external pure returns (uint256) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    function gaugeFees() external pure returns (uint256, uint256) {\n        return (0, 0);\n    }\n\n    function collectFees() external {}\n\n    function token0() external view returns (address) {\n        return token0Address;\n    }\n\n    function token1() external view returns (address) {\n        return token1Address;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockNFPM {\n    struct PositionData {\n        address owner;\n        address token0;\n        address token1;\n        int24 tickSpacing;\n        int24 tickLower;\n        int24 tickUpper;\n        uint128 liquidity;\n    }\n\n    address public immutable factoryAddress;\n    uint256 private nextId = 1;\n    mapping(uint256 => PositionData) private positionsData;\n    mapping(address => mapping(address => bool)) private approvals;\n\n    constructor(address factory_) {\n        factoryAddress = factory_;\n    }\n\n    function factory() external view returns (address) {\n        return factoryAddress;\n    }\n\n    function mintPosition(\n        address owner,\n        address token0,\n        address token1,\n        int24 tickSpacing,\n        int24 tickLower,\n        int24 tickUpper,\n        uint128 liquidity\n    ) external returns (uint256 tokenId) {\n        tokenId = nextId++;\n        positionsData[tokenId] = PositionData({\n            owner: owner,\n            token0: token0,\n            token1: token1,\n            tickSpacing: tickSpacing,\n            tickLower: tickLower,\n            tickUpper: tickUpper,\n            liquidity: liquidity\n        });\n    }\n\n    function ownerOf(uint256 tokenId) external view returns (address) {\n        return positionsData[tokenId].owner;\n    }\n\n    function setApprovalForAll(address operator, bool approved) external {\n        approvals[msg.sender][operator] = approved;\n    }\n\n    function isApprovedForAll(address owner, address operator) external view returns (bool) {\n        return approvals[owner][operator];\n    }\n\n    function positions(uint256 tokenId)\n        external\n        view\n        returns (\n            uint96,\n            address,\n            address,\n            address,\n            int24,\n            int24,\n            int24,\n            uint128,\n            uint256,\n            uint256,\n            uint128,\n            uint128\n        )\n    {\n        PositionData memory position = positionsData[tokenId];\n        require(position.owner != address(0), \"position missing\");\n        return (\n            0,\n            address(0),\n            position.token0,\n            position.token1,\n            position.tickSpacing,\n            position.tickLower,\n            position.tickUpper,\n            position.liquidity,\n            0,\n            0,\n            0,\n            0\n        );\n    }\n\n    function collect(INonfungiblePositionManager.CollectParams calldata params)\n        external\n        returns (uint256 amount0, uint256 amount1)\n    {\n        require(positionsData[params.tokenId].owner != address(0), \"position missing\");\n        return (0, 0);\n    }\n\n    function safeTransferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 tokenId) external {\n        PositionData storage position = positionsData[tokenId];\n        require(position.owner == from, \"not owner\");\n        require(msg.sender == from || approvals[from][msg.sender], \"not approved\");\n\n        position.owner = to;\n\n        if (to.code.length > 0) {\n            require(\n                IERC721Receiver(to).onERC721Received(msg.sender, from, tokenId, \"\") ==\n                    IERC721Receiver.onERC721Received.selector,\n                \"unsafe receiver\"\n            );\n        }\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockRHYBR {\n    uint256 public lastDeposited;\n    uint256 public lastRedeemedAmount;\n    uint8 public lastRedeemType;\n    address public lastRedeemRecipient;\n\n    function depostionEmissionsToken(uint256 amount) external {\n        lastDeposited = amount;\n    }\n\n    function redeemFor(uint256 amount, uint8 redeemType, address recipient) external {\n        lastRedeemedAmount = amount;\n        lastRedeemType = redeemType;\n        lastRedeemRecipient = recipient;\n    }\n}",
